<title>UK: Costain shareholders approve divestments.</title>
<headline>Costain shareholders approve divestments.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shareholders in Costain Group Plc on Friday approved the planned sale of the construction and engineering company's U.S. coal business and the divestment of the interest in the Spitalfields property development.</p>
<p>&quot;We now have the basis for the group to move forward, concentrating solely on its core engineering and construction business,&quot; chairman Christopher Benson said in a statement.</p>
<p>Costain said earlier this month that it was selling its U.S. coal units to Rencoal Inc of the U.S. for 28.6 million stg.</p>
<p>It also announced at the time that it would sell its one-third stake in the Spitalfields development site in central London to Malaysia's Metacorp for 23.4 million stg.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
